PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>

# Every *schema* term declared in the queried graph whose IRI belongs to a
# namespace this ecosystem owns: gcdfo: (DFO) or smn: (shared layer).
#
# "Schema" here means class or property. This is deliberately the subset of
# scripts/sparql/declared-owned-iris.rq that excludes owl:NamedIndividual, and
# it exists because the two kinds of declaration fail differently:
#
#   * A class or property declaration can appear *by accident*. The OWL API
#     supplies a declaration for any otherwise-untyped IRI used in class or
#     property position, so a module naming a term core has retired silently
#     re-mints it. That is ADR-008, and all seven terms in that incident were
#     owl:Class or owl:ObjectProperty. scripts/check-modules.sh requires this
#     query's delta against core to be empty, for every module, always.
#
#   * An individual declaration cannot appear that way. An untyped IRI in the
#     object position of an annotation property (skos:broader, skos:inScheme,
#     rdfs:seeAlso) mints nothing; an individual is declared only because a
#     module wrote `x a SomeClass`, which is an explicit act. A vocabulary
#     module does exactly that, 604 times on purpose, so check-modules judges
#     individuals by a different rule — see scripts/sparql/vocabulary-members.rq.
#
# External namespaces (sosa:, iadopt:, dwc:, prov:, ro:) are out of scope for
# the same reason as in declared-owned-iris.rq: alignment-research.ttl declares
# external class stubs on purpose, for WebVOWL readability. That exclusion
# retires if those stubs move out of the overlays.
#
# This query retires if the OWL API stops supplying declarations for untyped
# IRIs in class or property position — i.e. never in practice.
SELECT DISTINCT ?term
WHERE {
  VALUES ?type {
    owl:Class
    owl:ObjectProperty
    owl:DatatypeProperty
    owl:AnnotationProperty
  }

  ?term a ?type .

  FILTER(
    STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/gcdfo/salmon#") ||
    STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/smn/")
  )
}
ORDER BY ?term
